4. Certain activities to be exempt from unfair trade practice .–Permitting of the following activities carried
out for promoting directly or indirectly the sale, use or supply of any product or any business interest shall be
exempt from the purview of unfair trade practices, namely:–
(a) lotteries allowed under the Lotteries (Regulation) Act, 1998 (17 of 1998); and
(b) games of chance or skill not prohibited under the Public Gambling Act, 1867 (3 of 1867), which are
not gambling and wherein success depends on a substantial degree of skill and not chance.
